== Practice 4 — Writing for Subjects and Verbs (Larry's Bad Habit)

Missing words are in *bold*. Alternative answers are noted.

#block[
  1. My friend Larry has a bad habit. (OK)\
  2. He #strong[is] never on time to anything. (add "is")\
  3. #strong[He] arrives ten minutes late everywhere. (add "He")\
  4. Larry always #strong[has] an excuse. (add "has" \u2014 also possible: "gives", "offers")\
  5. "I missed the bus." (OK)\
  6. "My alarm clock didn't ring." (OK)\
  7. "My watch stopped." (OK)\
  8. "My mother telephoned me just as I was leaving." (OK)\
  9. He uses each excuse at least twice a week. (OK)\
  10. I know them all. (OK)\
  11. Whenever Larry rushes in \u2014 ten minutes late, of course \u2014 and starts to say, "Sorry I'm late, but I \u2026 " or "Sorry I'm late, but my \u2026 " or "Sorry I'm late, but my mother \u2026 ," I can finish the sentence for him. (OK \u2014 complex sentence, complete)\
  12. Larry's bad habit #strong[is] not a problem for me any longer. (add "is")\
  13. If the movie #strong[starts] at 7:00, I tell Larry it starts at 6:45. (add "starts" \u2014 also possible: "is")\
  14. Then he #strong[is] early! (add "is" \u2014 also possible: "arrives")\
]

