== Practice 5 — Identifying and Punctuating Sentences (My Neighbors)

14 sentences with correct capitals and periods:

1. A young couple from India lives next door to me.
2. The husband's name is Ajay.
3. The wife's name is Anjuli.
4. Everyone calls her Anju.
5. They have a young son and are expecting their second child in a few weeks.
6. They hope to have a girl this time.
7. Both Ajay and Anju have good jobs.
8. He is an executive in a computer company.
9. She is a computer programmer and works in our local hospital.
10. Anju is a wonderful cook.
11. She cooks mostly Indian food.
12. They sometimes invite neighbors on weekends for a potluck meal.
13. We all bring something to share.
14. It is fun to live next door to Ajay and Anju.

